From 900fce157791691525776760cf29fa68429fabea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:03:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Round 8: Store SIR generator columns as three fixed
 slots

Every SIR generator column holds its diagonal plus at most one infection
source and one recovery source. Store each column as three (source, kind)
slots in ascending source order, padded after the real entries with zero
weights, and handle the escaping sink after the loop, so the product has
no inner loop bounds or per-column sink branch. A padded slot adds +0.0 to
a non-negative sum and the first product equals 0.0 + product, so each
column's additions are unchanged; the projection tests still match the
vendored solver bit for bit.

Workload: serial (96 SIR candidates, one worker), matrix API on both
sides, 11 samples.
Before median: 3.025 ms. After median: 1.532 ms. Speedup: 1.97x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
